      "side": 1,
      "message": "My only thought would be to add a separate config for the recovery:  `CONFIG_POWER_SLEEP_FAILURE_RECOVERY` and disable it by default by adding `#undef CONFIG_POWER_SLEEP_FAILURE_RECOVERY` to include/configs.h  This would eliminate the need of touching coachz, burnet, corori, etc. Also this approach would keep sleep hang detection (without recovery) on the above boards, which I think is a benefit.\nYou\u0027ll just need to enable it in guybrush/baseboard.h to keep the behaviour on guybrush consistent.\nAnd then a follow-up CL to enable `CONFIG_POWER_SLEEP_FAILURE_RECOVERY`.",
      "parentUuid": "4334315a_beb627b5",
      "revId": "5934d4d6dd10cfb1b5e8708a5b56793b6a588e56",
